  "conclusion": "Large A9 16\u219232 independent-hit gain coincides with removal of earlier checksum\u2192partial-count\u2192hash BZHI feedback on both platforms and both loader routes. This comparison does not isolate SIMD selector width.",
  "static_findings": [
    "All16 selected complete hit CFGs are inline and call-free; no public body or timing wrapper boundary explains the gain.",
    "A9 composed16/direct16 carry RCX from previous payload checksum, write only CL=40, then consume RCX as BZHI count. Both32 variants consume RAX freshly defined by the key-multiplier constant before AL=40; the checksum edge is gone.",
    "A10 has no checksum-count feedback in all4 variants: its count register has a fresh constant producer.",
    "32-byte composed and direct loaders both collapse to a single memory-operand YMM VPCMPEQB at primary offset5 and secondary offset9; no residual separate low/high loads, VINSERT or helper boundary appears in these selected widened-read recipes.",
    "Zen5 wide compares use VPMOVMSKB; Granite uses an AVX-512 comparison mask followed by KMOVD.16-byte controls use XMM compares with VPMOVMSKB/KMOVW and clamp active count to16 before a guarded second group.",
    "Wide active-count BZHIL consumes a full-width bucket count definition. It is distinct from the problematic constant40-bit hash BZHI.",
    "Wide selector also replaces group-boundary traversal and failed-candidate ROL+AND bit clearing with one dense mask/loop and BTR. Those changes are real, but not independently cost-qualified here.",
    "Physical slot/unit/used-byte geometry and populations are identical across4 execution variants for each selected arm.32-byte reads remain in the same initialized stable128-byte bucket, with inactive lanes masked before suffix access."
  ],
  "mask_control_advice": [
    "Prefer split/paired controls with64-bit opaque count output plus explicit BZHI asm. MOVL-to-intrinsic alone is only a hint; a later compiler partial-byte rematerialization can reintroduce the edge.",
    "Paired count output must be early-clobber because it is written before x is consumed; final result may overlap inputs read before its write.",
    "Keep pure asm nonvolatile and without memory clobber; use cc clobber for BZHI/AND. Audit any extra TEST because opaque asm does not preserve LLVM flag semantics.",
    "Preserve independently proved upper-zero facts after masking; retain Width0 and Width>=64 semantics before low8 BZHI counts, including runtime widths>=256. Do not narrow accepted key semantics.",
    "Opaque controls can stop folding key producer domain mask into seeded split mask, creating extra masks/MOVs. Charge complete producer+split, hoisting and spills. Split count can hoist independently; paired MOV cannot.",
    "Ensure ordinary/exact Abseil sees identical controlled key generation, or explicitly retain a fixed baseline and report added key-generation cost. Do not use only baseline ratios to hide intervention overhead.",
    "Compare complete operations after source-level interventions; do not presume binary-patch instruction parity or attribute a32-only improvement to selector width."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The static checksum edge is established. Scheduling cost and its dominance remain inference pending matched count-only intervention on these actual complete consumers.",
    "No new serial disassembly diagnosis in this receipt; serial rows are timing context from the owning campaign. Historical_bridge separately retains complete serial CFGs.",
    "No cycle/resource/cache/DRAM causality or architecture/preset selection claimed. K16 gains are outside this bounded K40 audit.",
    "Whole-body instruction/SP counts are not average dynamic work; occupied ranks, collisions and secondary frequency differ between A9/A10 geometry."
  ]
}
